          "date": "2026-11-06 02:13:31.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: shorten sanity test_834",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: shorten sanity test_834\n\ntest_834 truncates a 100 MB file to 5 GB and reads all of it\nthrough fio with the mmap engine and MADV_HUGEPAGE. The read\nof the sparse hole runs at about 33 MiB/s, so the test spends\nabout 157 seconds of its 190 second CI average in fio.\n\nTruncate to 512 MB instead. That is still far larger than the\nreadahead window and a 2 MB huge page, and the fio read still\ncrosses the data and hole boundary with MADV_HUGEPAGE set.\n\nOn a local single node VM (1 MDT, 3 OSTs) the test went from\n261 and 240 seconds (the first run, 749 seconds, included a\ncold start) to 37, 22 and 27 seconds. With 15515 runs per 30\ndays and about 160 seconds saved per run, the expected CI\nsaving is about 690 hours per 30 days.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity env=ONLY=834\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I490cf77a18c332252a5e3277c6d12669bae8ad41\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70183\nReviewed-by: Alex Zhuravlev <azhuravlev@thelustrecollective.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
